==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|mēns}} {{m|la|rea|lit=guilty mind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌmɛnz ˈɹiːə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mentes reae}}
# {{label|en|general, psychology}} a [[reactive]] [[mind]], a conscious knowing by the individual that an act was omitted, either by themselves or by another
# {{label|en|legal}} a [[guilty]] [[mind]], a conscious knowing by the perpetrator that the act he/she committed was illicit

